cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these measurements, cite this record."
title: "Local LLM benchmarks on AMD Strix Halo (gfx1151), and the 16 GiB VRAM class"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Dom"
    alias: "barmynon"
    website: "https://github.com/barmynon"
date-released: 2026-11-10
url: "https://strix-halo-128-benchmarks.github.io/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/strix-halo-128-benchmarks/strix-halo-128-benchmarks.github.io"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Measured capability and throughput for open-weight local LLMs on a single AMD
  Strix Halo machine (Ryzen AI Max+ 395, 128 GB unified memory), on llama.cpp over
  Vulkan. HumanEval pass@1 and MMLU-Pro accuracy at stated token caps, IFEval,
  prefill and decode, all with build identity and quant per run; plus a roster
  defined by what fits a 16 GiB graphics card, with fit and KV-cache arithmetic,
  context budgets, thirteen 16 GB cards compared, and the platform differences
  between a unified APU, a discrete card and Apple Silicon. Every figure is
  traceable to a run id in the published catalogue.
keywords:
  - local LLM
  - llama.cpp
  - Strix Halo
  - gfx1151
  - Vulkan
  - HumanEval
  - MMLU-Pro
  - IFEval
  - GGUF quantisation
  - 16 GiB VRAM
